{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795427233,"nonce":"cWKUc4OnVzQyiN7gLZi5/VmGSBo=","title":"A scrollbar's auto-hide waits for unrelated frames, then its fade repaints the window in full","message":"After a wheel scroll of the cn_demo page, the page scrollbar stays visible while the window is idle. It fades only when something else starts frames again, for example a calendar swipe 3 s later, and each frame of that fade is a full paint of the page.\n\nSeen with the desktop scripted swipe (`BLINC_BENCH_WHEEL=.cn-calendar-months`, built at 57a32d64 plus the hook) and a temporary log in `tick_scroll_physics` (patch kept in the session scratchpad as diag_scrollbar.patch):\n\n- The page scroll (node 7v1) leaves `Scrolling` and its scrollbar stays in `ScrollbarState::Scrolling` with the show spring settled. No tick runs after that while the window is idle.\n- When the swipes start, ticks resume, `idle_time` passes `auto_dismiss_delay` (1.5 s), and the scrollbar goes `FadingOut`. That took 45 frames, with `on_rows=false`, so `scroll_off_rows_animating` is true and the present gate (`scroll_gliding`) takes a full paint on each of them.\n- Motion trace of the same run: the swipe that overlaps the fade is full-painted throughout; the swipes before and after are fast-path frames apart from the structural frame of each turn.\n\nTwo separate things:\n\n1. Bug. `ScrollPhysics::tick_scrollbar` advances `idle_time` by `dt` per tick, and the tick runs only on frames that get as far as `tick_scroll_physics`. Nothing schedules a frame for the auto-dismiss deadline, so the scrollbar does not hide on its own. It needs a timed wake at the deadline (the desktop loop has `WakeProxy::wake_at`), or the idle time measured from a timestamp instead of accumulated from ticks.\n2. Perf. A scrollbar opacity fade changes one thumb, but it marks the scroll as animating off rows, and that costs a full paint per frame for its whole length. The thumb could ride as its own row (3b364ef lists the scrollbar among what is declined today), or the fade could be excluded from the off-rows test when the offset is not moving.\n\nRelated: 3b364ef, 916db13, 288a87f.","files":null}]}